  "note": "Re-judged 2026-11-20 by an independent agent after df3221e7b8 changed TestRFC3948InitiatorSessionRefusesHeldInnerAddress. RFC 3948 Section 5.1: \"Because SGW will now see two possible SAs that lead to 10.1.2.3, it can become confused about where to send packets coming from Suzy's server.  Implementors MUST devise ways of preventing this from occurring.\" The only change is the startPeerSession call, which now takes a sessionSockets value in place of the separate socket arguments; the peers, the held inner address and the asserted refusal are unchanged, so the initiator session is still refused a Child SA whose inner pair another peer already holds. Every other tagged unit of the cross-peer inner-selector registry (dropForeignInnerOverlaps at narrowing, innerSelectorRegistry.beginInstall at install) is as the 2026-10-31 verdict judged it. Verdict stands.",
